Z||000000||Cooter||04-01-2001||03:24 PM||||If you do, how long does your oxygen sensors last? Mine eats one about every 3 months and it is getting pretty old. I won't even drive the truck anymore because every time I do, I have to order another sensor. <BR>Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||04-01-2001||05:07 PM||||Eating O2 sensors that fast is usually a sign that sensor toxic sealers have been used or there is a coolant leak. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||WKDFIRO||04-02-2001||01:52 AM||||Projection system???<P>The only time I had problems with O2 sensors was when they were melting all the time. Then I just went back to an AC/Delco sensor and haven't had a problem since.<P>I usually replace them every other year. (In tune with my smog checks.)||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cooter||04-02-2001||10:46 PM||||The engine is fresh, but had been run for a while with a carb before going with the fuel injection. I can't figure it out. I ran the carb with a generic O2 sensor to tune with and never burned one up. Now the $50++++ Holley sensors are not lasting at all. I think that I will just run a non heated sensor with it and see how long it lasts.||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||04-03-2001||08:03 AM||||my dad's got a Projection system on his boat. (Supra skier) and he's happy with it... been on for over 70 hours and not a single problem. (not sure how many miles that equals) ||||reg||1
